  "notes": "USAGE:\n{模倣|もほう} is more formal than {真似|まね} (imitation/mimicry). It is commonly used in academic, artistic, and media contexts. It can function as a suru-verb: {模倣|もほう}する (to imitate).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {模倣|もほう}する (to imitate)\n- {模倣|もほう}{犯罪|はんざい} (copycat crime)\n- {模倣|もほう}{品|ひん} (imitation product, counterfeit)\n- {模倣|もほう}{者|しゃ} (imitator)\n- {模倣|もほう}から{始|はじ}まる (start from imitation)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{真似|まね} is the everyday word for \"imitation\" or \"mimicry\" and is less formal. {模写|もしゃ} specifically refers to copying a painting or artwork. {偽造|ぎぞう} means \"forgery\" or \"counterfeiting\" and implies illegal intent.",
